cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its frozen 2026 market data in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Risk-Aware Trading Agents: AI trading agents for US stocks with point-in-time news backtesting"
type: software
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24202496"
authors:
  - name: "Risk-Aware Trading Agents contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jackson-cmd/risk-aware-trading-agents"
url: "https://jackson-cmd.github.io/risk-aware-trading-agents/"
license: MIT
version: "0.8.0"
date-released: "2026-11-14"
abstract: >-
  Open-source AI trading agents for US stocks that read the macro calendar, the VIX term structure and
  cross-verified news before they buy, with backtesting, paper and live trading on 10 brokers, and an MCP
  server for LLM assistants. The research kit ships frozen, point-in-time copies of the 2026, 2022 and 2020
  markets (daily prices for 64 stocks and 25 ETFs and the VIX term structure; the news headlines are not
  redistributed) with SHA-256 hashes, a look-ahead check that re-runs every experiment with a random future, and
  tools to let LLM trading agents trade the period step by step.
keywords:
  - trading agents
  - news backtesting
  - look-ahead bias
  - point-in-time data
  - LLM agents
  - backtesting
  - algorithmic trading
  - risk management
  - VIX
  - MCP
